From be42f63bc30e3097c405bfd016bec1259373369e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 23:00:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 220/225] perf: bound the SVO RT pool upload and stop it
 running inside the sync update spin

Report 06c ranked S1 first: RTUploadDirtySlices ran from CheckUpdateMeshPools,
which CSvoEnv::Render called twice, which the stock CrySleep(5) sync update spin
called ~130 times per frame id. Every call handed multi megabyte regions to
CTexture::UpdateTextureRegion, which off the render thread copies the region into
a std::vector and appends a command to the FILL buffer - a buffer that cannot be
consumed until a frame boundary the spin never reaches. Hundreds of MB/s of
retained allocation, gigabytes over a long re-voxelization, which is why the
stall was machine wide and not engine wide.

- CheckUpdateMeshPools is now gated on the main frame id, so the upload, the
  deferred chunk frees and the stats log run exactly once per RENDERED frame.
- the second CheckUpdateMeshPools call in CSvoEnv::Render is removed (F3).
- new cvar e_svoTI_RT_UploadBudgetMB (default 8) caps the bytes submitted per
  frame; the dirty bitset became a per slice frame stamp so the budget spends
  itself oldest first and no slice can starve. Adjacent dirty slices are still
  coalesced into one UpdateTextureRegion.
- the two pool textures are created EMPTY (nullptr data), like the stock SVO
  brick pools, instead of with the whole 64 MB mirror: that copy was a 128 MB
  main thread memcpy on the first RT frame (S4). The dirty slice path fills them.
- the 64 + 64 MB CPU mirrors are allocated by the new RTPrepareMirrors() on the
  main thread on the first RT frame, not by the first voxelization worker to
  commit a chunk while holding the pool lock in exclusive mode (S5/F7). The
  zeroing is kept - whole Z slices are uploaded, so unwritten padding must read
  as empty nodes, not as heap garbage - only its position moves.
- upload slices / bytes / ms are accumulated for the HUD and the log.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SCUvWGLCsqzm3VNMzp4uiS
